>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_TAC_WITH`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH : config_update list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample under per-call configuration updates.

`REFUTE_TAC_WITH updates` behaves as
`REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC (current_config updates)`: when the tactic is
applied, `updates` are applied to `!Refute.the_config` from left to
right.  `the_config` itself is unchanged.

### Failure

Fails only if the resulting `expect` field is not met.  An invalid
update, such as `upd_search (Only [])`, raises when it is built.

### Example

>>__ load "Refute";
>> g `!xs : num list. LENGTH xs < 3`;

>> e (Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH
        [Refute.upd_search (Refute.Only [Refute.Exhaustive]),
         Refute.upd_size 5]);
>>__ drop();

### See also

[`Refute.REFUTE_TAC`](#Refute.REFUTE_TAC),
[`Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC`](#Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC),
[`Refute.config`](#Refute.config).
